# UX Designer Agent Gotchas

> Common mistakes and pitfalls in UX design

## Accessibility Gotchas

### Color-Only Information
**Problem:** Conveying status only through color
```
# WRONG
Red = error, Green = success (colorblind users can't distinguish)

# RIGHT
Red + "Error" icon + text message
Green + "Success" icon + text message
```

### Missing Alt Text
**Problem:** Images without descriptions
**Solution:** All images need meaningful alt text

### Poor Contrast
**Problem:** Text hard to read
**Solution:** Minimum 4.5:1 contrast ratio for normal text

### Keyboard Traps
**Problem:** Can't escape modal with keyboard
**Solution:** Escape key closes modals, focus returns to trigger

### Missing Focus Indicators
**Problem:** Can't see which element is focused
**Solution:** Visible focus ring on all interactive elements

## Form Design Gotchas

### Unclear Error Messages
**Problem:** "Invalid input" without explanation
**Solution:** Specific message: "Email must include @"

### Lost User Input
**Problem:** Form clears on validation error
**Solution:** Preserve all input, only highlight errors

### No Progress Indication
**Problem:** Long forms without progress feedback
**Solution:** Show step indicators, save progress

### Confusing Required Fields
**Problem:** Users don't know what's required
**Solution:** Mark required fields clearly, explain format

## Layout Gotchas

### Mobile Afterthought
**Problem:** Desktop-first design breaks on mobile
**Solution:** Design mobile-first, enhance for desktop

### Tiny Touch Targets
**Problem:** Buttons too small on mobile
**Solution:** Minimum 44x44px touch targets

### Hidden Navigation
**Problem:** Users can't find features
**Solution:** Don't hide critical navigation behind hamburgers

### Inconsistent Spacing
**Problem:** Visual chaos from random spacing
**Solution:** Use consistent spacing scale (4px, 8px, 16px...)

## Interaction Gotchas

### Hover-Only Interactions
**Problem:** Features only accessible on hover
**Solution:** All interactions must work on touch devices

### No Loading Feedback
**Problem:** User doesn't know if action worked
**Solution:** Show loading state immediately on action

### Destructive Actions Without Confirmation
**Problem:** One click deletes everything
**Solution:** Confirm destructive actions, allow undo

### Auto-Playing Media
**Problem:** Unexpected audio/video
**Solution:** Never autoplay media with sound

## Content Gotchas

### Jargon and Technical Terms
**Problem:** Users don't understand terminology
**Solution:** Use plain language, explain technical terms

### Walls of Text
**Problem:** Too much text, users don't read
**Solution:** Break into chunks, use bullets, highlight key info

### Missing Empty States
**Problem:** Blank page when no data
**Solution:** Helpful message explaining what to do

### Unclear CTAs
**Problem:** "Submit" doesn't explain what happens
**Solution:** Action-specific labels: "Create Account", "Send Message"

## Feedback Gotchas

### Silent Failures
**Problem:** Action fails with no indication
**Solution:** Always show error state with explanation

### Success Without Confirmation
**Problem:** User unsure if action completed
**Solution:** Confirm success with toast/message

### Ambiguous Status
**Problem:** User can't tell current state
**Solution:** Clear visual indicators for all states

## Component Gotchas

### Inconsistent Components
**Problem:** Same action looks different in different places
**Solution:** Use design system, consistent patterns

### Wrong Component Choice
**Problem:** Using dropdown for 2 options
**Solution:** Radio buttons for few options, dropdown for many

### Modal Overuse
**Problem:** Every action opens a modal
**Solution:** Modals for critical decisions only

## Testing Gotchas

### Only Testing Happy Path
**Problem:** Missing error states, edge cases
**Solution:** Test all states: empty, loading, error, success

### Not Testing on Real Devices
**Problem:** Works in simulator, fails on device
**Solution:** Test on actual phones, tablets

### Ignoring Slow Connections
**Problem:** Assumes fast network
**Solution:** Test on throttled connections

